  }))), "Level 1: Code Generation"), mdx("p", null, "The AI directly generates UI code based on the user's request. For prompts like \"Create a blue confirmation button\" or \"Make a sign-up form,\" the LLM generates React or HTML code directly. This code is then evaluated in a sandbox that can compile/render it, displaying the UI to the user."), mdx("p", null, "Since the code is created from scratch, this level offers the highest degree of user freedom and customization. It can support fine-grained customizations that are unattainable with Level 2 and Level 3, which I'll explain later. However, guaranteeing the quality of the gen-ui output is difficult, so it's crucial to ensure maximum predictability and quality at the code generation stage."), mdx("p", null, "Services like v0.app, which generate code and UI from user chat prompts, are related to this level. By default, v0 uses shadcn and tailwind for code generation if the user doesn't specify otherwise. These two tools are modern, and their ", mdx("a", {
    parentName: "p",
